From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Homura <egzozu.be.bas@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] clangd: avoid a thread-local destructor in the root Context

Hexagon's R_HEX_B22_PCREL has +-8MB reach and lld has no thunk for it.
In a static clangd link the call from libc++abi's __cxa_thread_atexit to
the C library's __cxa_thread_atexit_impl is out of range, so the link
fails with

  relocation R_HEX_B22_PCREL out of range ... references
  '__cxa_thread_atexit_impl'

The only nontrivial C++ thread_local destructor linked into clangd is the
root Context. Keep the thread-local pointer but leak the empty root; it
holds no context data, and losing one shared_ptr per thread costs less
than dropping the whole tool for such a target.
---
diff --git a/clang-tools-extra/clangd/support/Context.cpp b/clang-tools-extra/clangd/support/Context.cpp
--- a/clang-tools-extra/clangd/support/Context.cpp
+++ b/clang-tools-extra/clangd/support/Context.cpp
@@ -20,7 +20,9 @@ Context Context::clone() const { return Context(DataPtr); }
 
 static Context &currentContext() {
-  static thread_local auto C = Context::empty();
-  return C;
+  static thread_local Context *C = nullptr;
+  if (!C)
+    C = new Context(Context::empty());
+  return *C;
 }
 
 const Context &Context::current() { return currentContext(); }
